From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ship the GPL-2.0-only COPYING in the wheel's dist-info

pyproject.toml declares `license` as the legacy `{ text = ... }` table,
which meson-python's build backend (via pyproject-metadata) never pairs
with any default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING* glob -- it only ever includes files
named in `license-files`. As a result every wheel upstream publishes
(verified against the real
beancount-3.2.3-cp312-cp312-manylinux2014_x86_64.manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
from PyPI) carries no licence file at all.

pyproject-metadata also refuses `license-files` outright unless `license`
is itself a PEP 639 SPDX expression string, not the old table form. The
text was already valid SPDX, just wrapped in the deprecated table, so the
fix is two coupled edits: turn `license` into the plain SPDX string and
add `license-files = ["COPYING"]`. meson-python then copies the
repository's root COPYING into dist-info/licenses/COPYING.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; no fork of beancount/beancount to push from]
---
 pyproject.toml | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index b1b6eec..1a14ece 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@ external data into one's input file in Beancount syntax.""" }
 authors = [
     { name = "Martin Blais", email = "blais@furius.ca" },
 ]
-license = { text = "GPL-2.0-only" }
+license = "GPL-2.0-only"
+license-files = ["COPYING"]
 requires-python = ">=3.9"
 dependencies = [
     "click >=7.0",
--
